Description: local control center for Linux single-board computers
 rsetup-next provides one typed control plane for observing and managing a
 Linux single-board computer. It includes a scriptable command-line interface,
 an interactive terminal interface, and a loopback Web control center.
 .
 Mutating operations are dry-run by default and require explicit live execution
 and confirmation.

Package: rsetup-controller
Priority: optional
# 与 rsetup-next 同一架构口径：仅维护 64 位 amd64/arm64，不做 Architecture: any。
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 adduser,
 ca-certificates,
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests:
 mariadb-server,
 nginx,
Description: Web control center (controller) for rsetup-next
 rsetup-controller is the standalone HTTP control-plane process of rsetup-next:
 it serves the embedded web UI and its typed API from a loopback listener
 (127.0.0.1:8080 by default) on top of a MySQL/MariaDB or TiDB database. It
 terminates no TLS and is not designed for exposure to untrusted networks.
 .
 The package installs the binaries, one systemd unit and a configuration
 template, and configures or enables nothing: an operator must fill in
 /etc/default/rsetup-controller (database URL, allowed Host list, allowed
 browser Origin, management cursor secret), migrate the target database with
 rsetup-controller-migrate, and only then start the service.
 .
 The unit drops privileges to the static system account rsetup-controller,
 which the package creates on install (adduser --system) so that
 /var/lib/rsetup-controller keeps one stable owner across restarts.

Package: rsetup-board-agent
Priority: optional
# 与其余两个包同一架构口径：仅维护 64 位 amd64/arm64，不做 Architecture: any。
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: board-side agent for rsetup-next
 rsetup-board-agent is the agent process intended to run on a managed single
 board: it answers the controller's typed read-only queries (capabilities,
 device status, clock, durable task journal) from a local, read-only source and
 keeps a durable task journal under its own state directory.
 .
 The shipped binary is a read-only sampling agent. The production encrypted
 tunnel is not wired up yet (the wire protocol codec is not approved), and a
 real host reboot boundary is not implemented: both reboot actions answer
 "capability unavailable" and the process never reboots the machine. The systemd
 unit runs it as root in the read-only watch loop, because reading the board's
 full hardware state requires root privileges.
